' Handling input events in VBR (Godot slice 7).
'
' `On Input(event)` runs on every input event Godot delivers — key presses, mouse
' clicks, gamepad. The `event` is an InputEvent object you query; the cleanest
' check is by *action* (mapped in Godot's Input Map), so it works for keyboard and
' pad alike. Lowers to gdext `fn input(&mut self, event: Gd<InputEvent>)`.
'
' (For continuous movement, poll `Input.IsPressed` in `On Process` instead — see
' godot_player.vbr. `On Input` is for discrete, one-shot events.)

Node2D "Controller"
    On Input(event)
        If event.IsActionPressed("ui_accept") Then
            Debug.Print "accept pressed"
        End If
        If event.IsActionPressed("ui_cancel") Then
            Debug.Print "cancel pressed"
        End If
    End Input
End Node2D
